MIDWAY CAMPAIGN — HOW TO PLAY
{PAGE}
THE STORY
June 1942. You command the U.S. Navy at Midway.
Japan is trying to take the island. Stop them.

Your forces:
  TF-16  Enterprise (E) and Hornet (H)
  TF-17  Yorktown (Y)
  Midway Island (M) with its own planes

Time runs in ticks (about 30-60 minutes each).
Type a command, then press ENTER, or type 1-9 to
wait that many hours.
{PAGE}
THE SCREEN
Top line: day and clock.
Second line: damage totals for Japan, U.S., Midway.

Map (rows below the header):
  1 = Japanese carriers (when spotted)
  2 = Japanese transports
  3 = Japanese cruisers
  4 = Task Force 17
  5 = Task Force 16
  6 = Midway Island
  * = a force that has been spotted

Right side: headings (HDG) and contacts.
  Heading 0=N  90=E  180=S  270=W
  Contact CV/TT/CA = identified; ?? = seen but not ID'd

Deck line (above the prompt):
  ENT/HOR/YOR/MID then C F S T counts
  C=CAP fighters  F=F4F ready  S=SBD  T=TBD
  Damage: under 60=OK, 60+=disabled, 100=sunk
{PAGE}
COMMANDS (type these at the CMD prompt)
  T   Set a task-force course
  A   Arm a strike on a carrier deck
  L   Launch that strike at a spotted target
  CA  Put F4F fighters on Combat Air Patrol
  CL  Clear the flight deck (return planes to ready)
  1-9 Wait that many hours (time passes, scouts, fights)
  ENTER  Wait one short tick (0 hours)
  ? or H  Show this help again

Planes:
  F4F = fighter (escort and CAP)
  SBD = dive bomber (your best weapon)
  TBD = torpedo bomber (hits are rare)
{PAGE}
HOW TO TYPE EACH COMMAND
T — Course
  Ask which TF: 16 or 17
  Then course 0 to 360 degrees

A — Arm a strike
  Pick carrier: E H Y or M
  Enter three numbers: F4F,SBD,TBD
  Example: 10,21,0
  SBDs need about one tick to finish arming
  (S count shows 1000+ while still arming)

CA — Combat Air Patrol
  Pick carrier, then how many F4F for CAP
  Keep at least 5 CAP on each carrier if you can

CL — Clear deck
  Pick carrier; armed planes go back to ready pools

L — Launch
  Pick carrier with a ready strike
  If several targets, pick target number 1..N
  Max launch range is about 200 nautical miles
  No launches or landings at night
{PAGE}
STRATEGY
* SBDs do the real damage; U.S. torpedoes rarely hit.
* Keep CAP up — it stops Japanese strikes.
* Launch soon after arming; bombs on deck can explode
  if the ship is hit.
* Steer toward contacts with T.
* Scouts work from about 4 AM to 7 PM.
* Win by sinking Akagi, Kaga, Soryu, and Hiryu,
  and by protecting Midway Island.
{END}
